      <h2>The Low-Sugar Dessert Protocol: Satisfying Cravings Under 250 Calories</h2>
      <p>Denying yourself a treat at Dairy Queen is completely unnecessary. The key is recognizing the stark glycemic divide between pre-portioned novelty bars and soft-serve spindle blends:</p>

      <div style="background:#FAF7F2;border:1px solid #EDE4D6;border-radius:18px;padding:24px;margin:24px 0;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#0B1E38;font-size:1.2rem;">The 4 Best Portion-Controlled Desserts</h3>
        <ul style="margin:12px 0 0 0;padding-left:0;list-style:none;">
          <li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #EBE1D2;">
            <strong>1. The Classic Dilly® Bar (210 Calories | 16g Sugar):</strong> 
            A pre-molded disk of vanilla soft serve dipped in crisp confectionery coating. Because it is frozen on a wooden stick, portion creep is impossible.
          </li>
          <li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #EBE1D2;">
            <strong>2. Kids' Vanilla Soft Serve Cone (170 Calories | 4.5g Fat | 19g Sugar):</strong> 
            Provides the full parlor sensory experience of cold, velvety soft serve with zero guilt.
          </li>
          <li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #EBE1D2;">
            <strong>3. Non-Dairy Gluten-Free Dilly Bar (240 Calories | 15g Sugar):</strong> 
            Crafted with coconut cream base and vegan chocolate shell, ideal for lactose-sensitive diners.
          </li>
          <li style="padding:10px 0;">
            <strong>4. Small Strawberry Sundae (230 Calories | 6g Fat):</strong> 
            Selecting strawberry topping instead of heavy cocoa fudge cuts saturated fat by nearly 65%.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Blizzard Caloric Spectrum: How to Order Without Blowing Your Macro Budget</h2>
      <p>If your heart is set on a blended Blizzard, apply these laboratory guidelines:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strict Mini-Only Rule:</strong> A Mini Blizzard contains 6 fluid ounces. Choosing an <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Mini</a> (380 cal) instead of a Large (1,050 cal) saves an astonishing <strong>670 calories</strong>—the equivalent of an entire second meal.</li>
        <li><strong>Favor Fruit &amp; Aerated Candy Over Cookie Dough:</strong> Flavors like Strawberry Cheesequake (~330 cal in Mini) or Butterfinger (~350 cal) carry significantly lower fat content than dense oil-shortened doughs like Choco Brownie Extreme (~400 cal) or Reese's Peanut Butter Cup (~380 cal).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Keto &amp; Low-Carb Drive-Thru Playbook</h2>
      <p>Eating ketogenic or low-carb at a DQ Grill &amp; Chill is surprisingly straightforward when you use the following ordering vernacular:</p>
      <div style="background:#F0FDF4;border-left:4px solid #16A34A;padding:18px 22px;border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;margin:20px 0;">
        <p style="margin:0;font-weight:700;color:#14532D;font-size:1.05rem;">The "No-Bun Salad Bowl" Order:</p>
        <p style="margin:6px 0 0 0;font-style:italic;color:#166534;">"Could I please get a Double Bacon Stackburger, but served protein-style in a bowl with no bun, no ketchup, extra pickles, and a side of yellow mustard?"</p>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;color:#14532D;font-size:0.9rem;"><strong>Macro Yield:</strong> ~540 Calories · 38g Protein · 42g Healthy Lipids · <strong>under 3g Net Carbs</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Sodium &amp; Side-Item Traps to Avoid</h2>
      <p>While calories are manageable, fast food sodium is a silent issue. Keep these two hazards in mind:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Cheese Curd Pitfall:</strong> While <a href="/items/cheese-curds">Wisconsin Cheese Curds</a> seem like a quick snack, a regular serving packs over 520 calories, 34g of fat, and a staggering 1,120mg of sodium.</li>
        <li><strong>Gravy vs. Picante Salsa:</strong> Swapping the 4 oz Country Gravy cup (130 cal, 560mg sodium) for two packets of mild picante salsa (20 cal, 180mg sodium) dramatically cleanses your macro profile.</li>
      </ul>

